Branching Patterns


One-way decision
if condition:
    statements
Run the block only when the condition is True.

Two-way decision
if condition:
    statements
else:
    other_statements
Exactly one branch runs.

Multiple alternatives
if condition_1:
    statements
elif condition_2:
    other_statements
else:
    fallback_statements
Python selects the first true branch.

Pattern 3: Build a New String
word = "Hello"
modified = ""

for char in word:
    if char in "aeiouAEIOU":
        modified += "*"
    else:
        modified += char

print(modified)
The result is H*ll*. Each iteration contributes one character to the new string.

